.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH tomat-watch 1  "watch " 
.SH NAME
watch \- Continuously output status updates
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwatch\fR [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-interval\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Continuously watch and output timer status updates. This maintains a single connection to the daemon and updates at the specified interval. Automatically exits when the daemon stops. More efficient than polling with \*(Aqstatus\*(Aq command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR [default: waybar]
Output format: waybar, i3status\-rs, or plain
.br

.br
[\fIpossible values: \fRwaybar, i3status\-rs, plain]
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
Custom text format (e.g. "{icon} {time}")
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interval\fR \fI<INTERVAL>\fR [default: 0.25]
Update interval in seconds
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:

    # Watch with default interval (0.25 seconds)
    tomat watch

    # Watch with 5\-second updates
    tomat watch \-\-interval 5

    # Watch with plain text output
    tomat watch \-\-output plain
